cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite this repository."
title: "RHShortIntervals: psi(x) = x + O(x^(1/2+delta)) and primes in short intervals from the Riemann Hypothesis, in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof that Mathlib's RiemannHypothesis implies
  psi(x) = x + O(x^(1/2+delta)) and a prime in (x, x + x^(1/2+epsilon)] for all large x
  (von Koch 1901), by a contour shift of the smoothed Chebyshev function of
  PrimeNumberTheoremAnd to the line Re s = 1/2 + delta.
type: software
authors:
